; expect 42
; stage1 lowers the effect system: evidence slots, dynamic dispatch,
; and the outward-dispatch rule. Every term below has a way to be
; wrong that a simpler program cannot see, so the sum discriminates:
;
;   a  dispatch is DYNAMIC, not lexical - `helper` names no handler
;      and still reaches the one installed around its caller;
;   b  nesting shadows and restores - the inner handler wins while its
;      handle is live and the outer answers again after it exits, so a
;      lowering that forgot the restore gives 202 here, not 302;
;   c  a handler performing its own effect dispatches OUTWARD, because
;      it runs under the evidence in scope at its INSTALLATION. The
;      naive lowering re-enters the same handler forever;
;   d  a two-argument operation takes a CURRIED handler chain, one
;      argument per indirect call - applying both at once answers with
;      the inner closure's address;
;   e  a local shadowing an operation name binds the LOCAL, which is
;      how sema resolves it; a generator that dispatched the name
;      instead would trap with no handler installed.
(effect Ask
  (ask :: (-> Int Int)))

(effect Two
  (two :: (-> Int Int Int)))

(:: helper (-> Int Int))
(fn (helper n)
  (ask n))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (let ((a (handle (helper 5) (Ask) (lambda (x) (* x 2)))))
    ; The outer lists name `Alloc` because a nested `handle` in the
    ; body heap-allocates its own evidence record, which is an effect
    ; the enclosing handle has to cover - AX3011 otherwise, in both
    ; compilers.
    (let ((b (handle
               (+ (handle (ask 1) (Ask) (lambda (x) (+ x 100)))
                  (ask 1))
               (Ask Alloc)
               (lambda (x) (+ x 200)))))
      (let ((c (handle
                 (handle (ask 3) (Ask) (lambda (x) (ask (+ x 1))))
                 (Ask Alloc)
                 (lambda (x) (* x 10)))))
        (let ((d (handle (two 6 7) (Two) (lambda (p) (lambda (q) (* p q))))))
          (let ((e (let ((ask (lambda (x) (- x 1)))) (ask 4))))
            (if (== (+ (+ (+ (+ a b) c) d) e) 397) 42 1)))))))
